  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The review is based on a framework that has been predominantly developed and referenced within a German planning context, which may limit its immediate applicability to other planning cultures.",
      "what": "This systematic review evaluates the Mobility Culture Framework (MCF), a planning and research tool developed primarily in Germany that analyzes mobility cultures through the interaction of social conditions and built environments. The review identifies theoretical, methodological, and empirical gaps in the existing literature, focusing on how the framework has been applied and conceptualized.",
      "why": "It establishes that the framework's conceptual foundations are frequently misunderstood or lost in translation, and argues for integrating mixed-method approaches and expanding research beyond large metropolitan areas to make the framework a more robust transformative planning tool."
    }
